{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"815b1666-2286-4d8e-b263-2d1e2a4b9fc0","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the 500 error on the second publish has been identified and fixed. Detailed findings and documentation have been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-jCZlyI/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n- **Cause**: On the first publish, the table is empty, so `related()` returns an empty list (`similar: []`). On the second publish, existing stories are found and `similarity()` returns a Python `float`. Boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects Python `float` types with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.`, causing the unhandled exception and returning HTTP 500.\n- **Fix**:\n  1. Updated [`similarity()`](file:///tmp/h-jCZlyI/src/app.py#L25-L33) in [src/app.py](file:///tmp/h-jCZlyI/src/app.py) to return a `Decimal(str(score))` instead of a raw `float`.\n  2. Added test coverage in [tests/test_publish.py](file:///tmp/h-jCZlyI/tests/test_publish.py) verifying that subsequent publishes compute similarities and save to DynamoDB without error.\n","duration_seconds":71.794208,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":169650,"output_tokens":2586,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":100176,"total_tokens":172236}}}
